# core.autocrlf is true on this machine, so a checked-out shell script would carry
# CRLF and Git Bash would die on the \r in the shebang before the first command.
# Scoped to *.sh on purpose: the PowerShell and Python tools are unaffected and
# stay exactly as they are.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Patch files must keep their LF line terminators. A patch whose own lines end in
# CRLF does not apply -- measured 2026-08-05: the three group patches converted to
# CRLF made tools/verify-patch-groups.sh go red across all six orders. CR inside
# the described content is fine and expected (crow-lab/src is checked out CRLF);
# it is the framing that has to stay LF. -text so git never rewrites either side.
*.patch -text
